module communityCompositionDetection
module monospeciesGrowthDetection
module exoMetabolomicsDetection

// ============================================================
// Deciphering Microbial Interactions in Synthetic Human Gut
// Microbiome Communities
// Venturelli et al., Mol. Syst. Biol. (2018) 14: e8157
// DOI: 10.15252/msb.20178157
//
// EXPERIMENTAL OVERVIEW:
// A 12-member synthetic human gut community spanning Bacteroidetes
// (BT, BO, BU, BV), Firmicutes (BH, CH, ER, FP), Actinobacteria
// (CA, EL), and Proteobacteria (DP), plus Prevotella copri (PC).
//
// This protocol encodes three training datasets used to parameterise
// a generalised Lotka-Volterra (gLV) model of community dynamics:
//
//   PHASE 1 (M dataset)  : Monospecies growth characterisation.
//                          All 12 species grown individually.
//                          OD600 at ~30 min intervals, 16S rRNA at
//                          ~12 h intervals, serial 1:20 dilution
//                          every 24 h over 72 h (3 dilution cycles).
//
//   PHASE 2 (PW1 dataset): Pairwise co-cultures, 66 combinations,
//                          1:1 initial ratio by OD600.
//                          Same serial-transfer regime as Phase 1.
//
//   PHASE 3 (PW2 dataset): Subset of 15 pairwise communities
//                          inoculated at asymmetric initial species
//                          proportions (95:5 and 5:95 by OD600)
//                          to probe history-dependent behaviours.
//
//   PHASE 4 (Validation) : Full 12-member community + 12 single-
//                          species dropout communities (11-member).
//                          Used to validate gLV model predictions.
//
//   PHASE 5 (Metabolomics): Exo-metabolomics profiling of all 12
//                           monospecies using LC-MS/MS (97 metabolites,
//                           twofold threshold for utilisation/secretion).
//
// GROWTH CONDITIONS:
//   Anaerobic chamber (85% N2, 5% H2, 10% CO2), 37 C, no shaking.
//   Rich Anaerobic Basal Broth (ABB) media.
//   Serial transfer: 1:20 dilution into fresh ABB every 24 h.
//   Communities arrayed in 96-well deep-well plates (gas-permeable
//   seal). OD600 monitored in parallel 384-well plate at 30 min
//   intervals using Tecan Infinite F200 Pro.
//   16S rRNA gene sequencing: V3-V4 region, Illumina MiSeq,
//   dual-indexed primers, ~12 h sampling intervals.
//
// INOCULATION:
//   Slow-growth species (BH, FP, CA, PC, ER, DP): inoculated 41 h
//   before experiment start.
//   Fast-growth species (BU, BV, BT, BO, CH, EL): inoculated 16 h
//   before experiment start.
//   Each species: 0.01 OD600 from overnight starter culture in ABB.
//
// DILUTION SCHEME (BIOSCRIPT ABSTRACTION):
//   The 1:20 serial transfer at 24 h intervals is modelled as a
//   `mix` step (1 unit of community + 19 units of fresh ABB media)
//   at each transfer point. The OD600 monitoring (every 30 min)
//   and 16S rRNA sampling (~12 h) within each 24 h window are
//   represented as `detect` calls on the community droplets.
//   In the lilott8/BioScript compiler these produce distinct
//   basic blocks (BB) in the CFG, one per detect/heat/mix call.
//
// DURATION TOKENS:
//   BioScript accepts: s (seconds), m (minutes) only.
//   72 h total run = 4320 m (encoded per heat/incubation step).
//   30 min OD600 sampling = 30m.
//   12 h 16S sampling = 720m.
//   24 h transfer interval = 1440m.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                    -- device init; slow-growth starter
//                                   cultures for all 12 species
//   BB2  monospeciesGrowth       -- Phase 1: 12 monospecies runs,
//                                   OD600 + 16S, 3x serial transfer
//   BB3  monospeciesQC           -- QC gate on monospecies data quality
//   BB4  monoPass                -- monoQCSignal > 0: data accepted
//   BB5  monoFail                -- monoQCSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB6  monoJoin                -- join: pairwise branch begins
//   BB7  pairwisePW1             -- Phase 2: 1:1 pairwise, 66 combos
//                                   representative pair (BT+FP shown;
//                                   all 66 run in parallel off-chip)
//   BB8  pw1QC                   -- QC gate on PW1 data
//   BB9  pw1Pass                 -- pw1QCSignal > 0: proceed
//   BB10 pw1Fail                 -- pw1QCSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB11 pw1Join                 -- join: PW2 branch begins
//   BB12 pairwisePW2             -- Phase 3: 15 asymmetric pairs
//                                   representative pair (BO+BT 95:5)
//   BB13 pw2QC                   -- QC gate on PW2 data
//   BB14 pw2Pass                 -- pw2QCSignal > 0: proceed
//   BB15 pw2Fail                 -- pw2QCSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB16 pw2Join                 -- join: validation branch begins
//   BB17 fullCommunity           -- Phase 4a: full 12-member community
//   BB18 dropoutCommunity        -- Phase 4b: representative dropout
//                                   (EL- shown as most influential)
//   BB19 validationQC            -- QC gate on validation communities
//   BB20 validationPass          -- valQCSignal > 0: proceed
//   BB21 validationFail          -- valQCSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB22 validationJoin          -- join: metabolomics branch begins
//   BB23 metabolomics            -- Phase 5: exo-metabolomics on all
//                                   monospecies (DP excluded: lag too
//                                   long for 24 h sampling window)
//   BB24 metaQC                  -- QC gate on metabolomics data
//   BB25 metaPass                -- metaQCSignal > 0: dispose
//   BB26 metaFail                -- metaQCSignal <= 0: drain
//   BB27 finalCleanup            -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// Manifest: all reagents used across all phases
// ============================================================

// Species (all 12 members of the synthetic community)
manifest BT_Cells          // Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron (ATCC 29148)
manifest BO_Cells          // Bacteroides ovatus (ATCC 8483)
manifest BU_Cells          // Bacteroides uniformis (DSM 6597)
manifest BV_Cells          // Bacteroides vulgatus (ATCC 8482)
manifest BH_Cells          // Blautia hydrogenotrophica (DSM 10507)
manifest CA_Cells          // Collinsella aerofaciens (DSM 3979)
manifest CH_Cells          // Clostridium hiranonis (DSM 13275)
manifest DP_Cells          // Desulfovibrio piger (ATCC 29098)
manifest EL_Cells          // Eggerthella lenta (DSM 2243)
manifest ER_Cells          // Eubacterium rectale (ATCC 33656)
manifest FP_Cells          // Faecalibacterium prausnitzii (DSM 17677)
manifest PC_Cells          // Prevotella copri (DSM 18205)

// Media and reagents
manifest ABB_Media         // Anaerobic Basal Broth (Oxoid); rich media
manifest GlycerolStock     // 25% glycerol cryo-stocks for all species

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// Prepare starter cultures for all 12 species from glycerol
// stocks into 15 mL ABB in anaerobic chamber.
// Slow-growth species inoculated 41 h before experiment start;
// fast-growth species inoculated 16 h before experiment start.
// This ensures all species are in comparable growth phases at
// time zero of each community experiment.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STARTER CULTURES - Slow-growth species (41 h pre-incubation)
// BH, FP, CA, PC, ER, DP
// Inoculated from 25% glycerol stocks into 15 mL ABB at 37 C.
// No shaking; anaerobic chamber (85% N2, 5% H2, 10% CO2).
// Each normalised to 0.01 OD600 before community inoculation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

glycerolBH = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaBH    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterBH  = mix glycerolBH with mediaBH for 5s
heat starterBH at 37c for 2460m  // 41 h = 2460 m

glycerolFP = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaFP    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterFP  = mix glycerolFP with mediaFP for 5s
heat starterFP at 37c for 2460m

glycerolCA = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaCA    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterCA  = mix glycerolCA with mediaCA for 5s
heat starterCA at 37c for 2460m

glycerolPC = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaPC    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterPC  = mix glycerolPC with mediaPC for 5s
heat starterPC at 37c for 2460m

glycerolER = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaER    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterER  = mix glycerolER with mediaER for 5s
heat starterER at 37c for 2460m

glycerolDP = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaDP    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterDP  = mix glycerolDP with mediaDP for 5s
heat starterDP at 37c for 2460m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STARTER CULTURES - Fast-growth species (16 h pre-incubation)
// BU, BV, BT, BO, CH, EL
// ------------------------------------------------------------

glycerolBU = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaBU    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterBU  = mix glycerolBU with mediaBU for 5s
heat starterBU at 37c for 960m   // 16 h = 960 m

glycerolBV = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaBV    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterBV  = mix glycerolBV with mediaBV for 5s
heat starterBV at 37c for 960m

glycerolBT = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaBT    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterBT  = mix glycerolBT with mediaBT for 5s
heat starterBT at 37c for 960m

glycerolBO = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaBO    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterBO  = mix glycerolBO with mediaBO for 5s
heat starterBO at 37c for 960m

glycerolCH = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaCH    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterCH  = mix glycerolCH with mediaCH for 5s
heat starterCH at 37c for 960m

glycerolEL = dispense 1 units of GlycerolStock
mediaEL    = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
starterEL  = mix glycerolEL with mediaEL for 5s
heat starterEL at 37c for 960m

// ============================================================
// BB2: monospeciesGrowth
// PHASE 1 (M dataset): All 12 species as monocultures.
// Each inoculated at 0.01 OD600 into fresh ABB.
// Serial transfer: 1:20 dilution every 24 h (3 transfers over
// 72 h total). OD600 sampled every 30 min; 16S rRNA at ~12 h.
//
// BIOSCRIPT ABSTRACTION:
//   Each monospecies is represented as a scalar droplet.
//   Three rounds of: detect (OD600) -> detect (16S) ->
//   mix with fresh ABB (1:20 serial transfer) -> heat 24 h.
//   In practice all 12 monocultures run in parallel in a
//   96-well deep-well plate; BioScript encodes one species
//   (BT) in full detail as the representative monospecies
//   block. The same pattern applies to all 12 species.
//
// NOTE ON PARALLEL EXECUTION:
//   lilott8/BioScript does not have a native parallel
//   construct. Each of the 12 monospecies is encoded as an
//   independent variable (monoculture). The compiler will
//   schedule them into separate CFG branches. Off-chip,
//   the Biomek liquid-handling robot arrays all 96 conditions
//   simultaneously.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// MONOSPECIES: BT (Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron)
// Representative fast-growth species. Lowest CV in PW1,
// meaning its fitness is least altered by a second species.
// Initialised at 0.01 OD600 from starterBT.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mediaForBT  = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
monoBT      = mix starterBT with mediaForBT for 5s

// Transfer 1 (t=0 to t=24 h): OD600 + 16S at t~12 h, then dilute.
monoBT_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoBT for 720m
monoBT_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoBT for 720m

// Serial transfer 1: 1 unit community + 19 units fresh ABB = 1:20 dilution.
// NOTE: `mix` with 19 units of media abstracts the Biomek-mediated
// aliquot transfer into a fresh 96-well deep-well plate.
freshABB_BT1  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
monoBT_T2     = mix monoBT with freshABB_BT1 for 5s
heat monoBT_T2 at 37c for 720m  // remaining 12 h of 24 h window

// Transfer 2 (t=24 h to t=48 h): OD600 + 16S at t~36 h, then dilute.
monoBT_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoBT_T2 for 720m
monoBT_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoBT_T2 for 720m

freshABB_BT2  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
monoBT_T3     = mix monoBT_T2 with freshABB_BT2 for 5s
heat monoBT_T3 at 37c for 720m

// Transfer 3 (t=48 h to t=72 h): OD600 + 16S at t~60 h; final
// 16S read at t=72 h marks end of experiment.
monoBT_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoBT_T3 for 720m
monoBT_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoBT_T3 for 720m

// Final 12 h incubation to reach 72 h endpoint.
heat monoBT_T3 at 37c for 720m

// Final OD600 and 16S at t=72 h (endpoint).
monoBT_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoBT_T3 for 30s
monoBT_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoBT_T3 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// MONOSPECIES: FP (Faecalibacterium prausnitzii)
// Slow-growth species. Shows highest variability in absolute
// abundance across PW1 communities (bimodal CV distribution).
// Receives 5 positive inter-species interactions in gLV model
// (ecologically responsive species).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mediaForFP  = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
monoFP      = mix starterFP with mediaForFP for 5s

monoFP_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoFP for 720m
monoFP_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoFP for 720m

freshABB_FP1  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
monoFP_T2     = mix monoFP with freshABB_FP1 for 5s
heat monoFP_T2 at 37c for 720m

monoFP_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoFP_T2 for 720m
monoFP_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoFP_T2 for 720m

freshABB_FP2  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
monoFP_T3     = mix monoFP_T2 with freshABB_FP2 for 5s
heat monoFP_T3 at 37c for 720m

monoFP_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoFP_T3 for 720m
monoFP_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoFP_T3 for 720m

heat monoFP_T3 at 37c for 720m

monoFP_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoFP_T3 for 30s
monoFP_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoFP_T3 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// MONOSPECIES: EL (Eggerthella lenta)
// Key ecological driver: absence of EL (EL-) reduces community
// productivity by 28-46% across growth stages. EL has 6
// positive outgoing interactions (most of any species). Despite
// low monospecies fitness, EL is the most influential species
// in community assembly. Long-tail CV distribution in PW1.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

mediaForEL  = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
monoEL      = mix starterEL with mediaForEL for 5s

monoEL_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoEL for 720m
monoEL_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoEL for 720m

freshABB_EL1  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
monoEL_T2     = mix monoEL with freshABB_EL1 for 5s
heat monoEL_T2 at 37c for 720m

monoEL_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoEL_T2 for 720m
monoEL_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoEL_T2 for 720m

freshABB_EL2  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
monoEL_T3     = mix monoEL_T2 with freshABB_EL2 for 5s
heat monoEL_T3 at 37c for 720m

monoEL_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoEL_T3 for 720m
monoEL_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoEL_T3 for 720m

heat monoEL_T3 at 37c for 720m

monoEL_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoEL_T3 for 30s
monoEL_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on monoEL_T3 for 30s

// NOTE: Monospecies runs for BO, BU, BV, BH, CA, CH, DP, ER,
// and PC follow the identical pattern. Each is a scalar droplet
// initialised from its respective starterXX variable, subjected
// to 3 rounds of 16S+OD600 detect -> 1:20 dilution -> 24 h heat.
// They are omitted here to avoid repetition but are required
// for full M-dataset construction (all 12 monospecies).

// ============================================================
// BB3: monospeciesQC
// Aggregate OD600 and 16S final reads to QC data quality.
// monospeciesGrowthDetection module checks: growth curves
// captured, carrying capacities estimated, lag phases resolved.
// ============================================================

monoQCSignal = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on monoBT_T3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB4 / BB5: Monospecies QC gate
// Pass (BB4): monoQCSignal > 0 -> M dataset accepted; proceed.
// Fail (BB5): monoQCSignal <= 0 -> data quality insufficient; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB6 (monoJoin).
// ============================================================

if (monoQCSignal > 0) {
    dispose monoBT_T3
    dispose monoFP_T3
    dispose monoEL_T3
} else {
    drain monoBT_T3
    drain monoFP_T3
    drain monoEL_T3
}

// ============================================================
// BB6: monoJoin
// Dispose monospecies QC signal; proceed to PW1 branch.
// ============================================================

dispose monoQCSignal

// ============================================================
// BB7: pairwisePW1
// PHASE 2 (PW1 dataset): 66 pairwise combinations (C(12,2)=66).
// Initial species ratio: 1:1 by OD600 (each 0.01 OD600).
// Total initial OD600 per well = 0.02.
// Same serial-transfer protocol as monospecies (1:20, 24 h, 72 h).
//
// Biologically significant pairs (from gLV network, Fig 2C):
//   BT+FP: BT inhibits FP (negative outgoing from BT);
//          FP receives 5 positive interactions in full community.
//   CH+ER: exemplar of +/- coexistence motif (Fig 4B,C);
//          CH inhibits ER; ER positively stimulates CH.
//          Converges to ~1:1 ratio from both initial conditions.
//   EL+BH: mutualism (+/+); both enhanced. Highest pairwise
//          productivity compared to null model.
//   BT+BV: bidirectional inhibition (-/-); mutual competition;
//          lowest pairwise productivity among Bacteroides pairs.
//
// BIOSCRIPT ENCODING:
//   Three representative pairs are fully encoded. All 66 pairs
//   run in parallel on the Biomek-arrayed 96-well plate.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PW1 PAIR: BT + FP (1:1 ratio)
// BT = fast-growth (from starterBT); FP = slow-growth (starterFP).
// Mix 1:1 by OD600 into fresh ABB. Serial transfer x3 over 72 h.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pw1_BT   = dispense 1 units of BT_Cells
pw1_FP   = dispense 1 units of FP_Cells
abbPW1_1 = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media

pw1_BT_FP   = mix pw1_BT with pw1_FP for 5s
pw1_BT_FP_m = mix pw1_BT_FP with abbPW1_1 for 5s

// Transfer 1
pw1_BT_FP_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_BT_FP_m for 720m
pw1_BT_FP_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_BT_FP_m for 720m

freshABB_pw1_1  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw1_BT_FP_T2    = mix pw1_BT_FP_m with freshABB_pw1_1 for 5s
heat pw1_BT_FP_T2 at 37c for 720m

// Transfer 2
pw1_BT_FP_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_BT_FP_T2 for 720m
pw1_BT_FP_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_BT_FP_T2 for 720m

freshABB_pw1_2  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw1_BT_FP_T3    = mix pw1_BT_FP_T2 with freshABB_pw1_2 for 5s
heat pw1_BT_FP_T3 at 37c for 720m

// Transfer 3 + final read
pw1_BT_FP_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_BT_FP_T3 for 720m
pw1_BT_FP_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_BT_FP_T3 for 720m

heat pw1_BT_FP_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw1_BT_FP_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_BT_FP_T3 for 30s
pw1_BT_FP_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_BT_FP_T3 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PW1 PAIR: CH + ER (1:1 ratio)
// Exemplar +/- coexistence motif: CH inhibits ER (negative);
// ER stimulates CH (positive). Negative feedback loop enables
// robust coexistence over broad parameter range (Fig 4B-D).
// Converges to approximately equal ratio from distinct initial
// conditions (stable coexistence, ~24% of PW1 pairs).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pw1_CH   = dispense 1 units of CH_Cells
pw1_ER   = dispense 1 units of ER_Cells
abbPW1_2 = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media

pw1_CH_ER   = mix pw1_CH with pw1_ER for 5s
pw1_CH_ER_m = mix pw1_CH_ER with abbPW1_2 for 5s

pw1_CH_ER_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_CH_ER_m for 720m
pw1_CH_ER_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_CH_ER_m for 720m

freshABB_CH_ER1 = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw1_CH_ER_T2    = mix pw1_CH_ER_m with freshABB_CH_ER1 for 5s
heat pw1_CH_ER_T2 at 37c for 720m

pw1_CH_ER_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_CH_ER_T2 for 720m
pw1_CH_ER_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_CH_ER_T2 for 720m

freshABB_CH_ER2 = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw1_CH_ER_T3    = mix pw1_CH_ER_T2 with freshABB_CH_ER2 for 5s
heat pw1_CH_ER_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw1_CH_ER_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_CH_ER_T3 for 720m
pw1_CH_ER_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_CH_ER_T3 for 720m

heat pw1_CH_ER_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw1_CH_ER_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_CH_ER_T3 for 30s
pw1_CH_ER_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_CH_ER_T3 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PW1 PAIR: EL + BH (1:1 ratio)
// Mutualism (+/+): EL stimulates BH; BH stimulates EL.
// Highest pairwise productivity enhancement vs null model
// (positive productivity relative to monospecies sum).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pw1_EL   = dispense 1 units of EL_Cells
pw1_BH   = dispense 1 units of BH_Cells
abbPW1_3 = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media

pw1_EL_BH   = mix pw1_EL with pw1_BH for 5s
pw1_EL_BH_m = mix pw1_EL_BH with abbPW1_3 for 5s

pw1_EL_BH_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_EL_BH_m for 720m
pw1_EL_BH_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_EL_BH_m for 720m

freshABB_EL_BH1 = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw1_EL_BH_T2    = mix pw1_EL_BH_m with freshABB_EL_BH1 for 5s
heat pw1_EL_BH_T2 at 37c for 720m

pw1_EL_BH_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_EL_BH_T2 for 720m
pw1_EL_BH_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_EL_BH_T2 for 720m

freshABB_EL_BH2 = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw1_EL_BH_T3    = mix pw1_EL_BH_T2 with freshABB_EL_BH2 for 5s
heat pw1_EL_BH_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw1_EL_BH_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_EL_BH_T3 for 720m
pw1_EL_BH_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_EL_BH_T3 for 720m

heat pw1_EL_BH_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw1_EL_BH_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw1_EL_BH_T3 for 30s
pw1_EL_BH_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_EL_BH_T3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8: pw1QC
// QC gate on PW1 dataset: check that pairwise community
// compositions are resolved (species proportions at 72 h
// classifiable as dominance, coexistence, or history-dependent).
// ============================================================

pw1QCSignal = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw1_CH_ER_T3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB9 / BB10: PW1 QC gate
// Pass (BB9): pw1QCSignal > 0 -> all 66 pairs resolved; proceed.
// Fail (BB10): pw1QCSignal <= 0 -> data insufficient; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB11 (pw1Join).
// ============================================================

if (pw1QCSignal > 0) {
    dispose pw1_BT_FP_T3
    dispose pw1_CH_ER_T3
    dispose pw1_EL_BH_T3
} else {
    drain pw1_BT_FP_T3
    drain pw1_CH_ER_T3
    drain pw1_EL_BH_T3
}

// ============================================================
// BB11: pw1Join
// Dispose PW1 QC signal; proceed to PW2 branch.
// ============================================================

dispose pw1QCSignal

// ============================================================
// BB12: pairwisePW2
// PHASE 3 (PW2 dataset): 15 representative pairwise communities
// inoculated at asymmetric initial species proportions.
// Two inoculation conditions per pair:
//   Condition A: 95% species A, 5% species B (by OD600)
//                major  = 0.0158 OD600, minor = 0.0008 OD600
//   Condition B: 5% species A, 95% species B (reciprocal)
// This design probes history-dependent behaviours:
//   ~50% dominance, ~24% coexistence, ~12% history-dependence
//   across the 51 pairs evaluated (Fig 2B, Appendix Fig S5B).
//
// Representative pair: BO + BT (97:5 to 5:95 sweep).
// BO+BT shows history-dependence due to slow relaxation
// to monostable equilibrium (Fig 4A); NOT bistability.
//
// NOTE ON UNITS:
//   0.0158 and 0.0008 OD600 are the actual inoculation volumes
//   used in the paper (PW2 M&M: "major and minor strains
//   inoculated at 0.0158 and 0.0008 OD600, respectively").
//   In BioScript, `dispense 1 units` maps to one droplet;
//   the asymmetry is captured by the mix ratio (19:1 and 1:19),
//   abstracted as separate major/minor dispense + mix steps.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PW2 PAIR: BO + BT, Condition A (BO major, 95%; BT minor, 5%)
// BO dominates at t=0; both reach community structure at t=72 h.
// History-dependent: community structure at 72 h depends on
// initial proportion (slow convergence to monostable state).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pw2_BO_major = dispense 19 units of BO_Cells   // 95% component
pw2_BT_minor = dispense 1 units of BT_Cells    // 5% component
abbPW2_A     = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media

pw2_BO_BT_A   = mix pw2_BO_major with pw2_BT_minor for 5s
pw2_BO_BT_A_m = mix pw2_BO_BT_A with abbPW2_A for 5s

pw2_A_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_m for 720m
pw2_A_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_m for 720m

freshABB_pw2_A1 = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw2_BO_BT_A_T2  = mix pw2_BO_BT_A_m with freshABB_pw2_A1 for 5s
heat pw2_BO_BT_A_T2 at 37c for 720m

pw2_A_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_T2 for 720m
pw2_A_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_T2 for 720m

freshABB_pw2_A2 = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw2_BO_BT_A_T3  = mix pw2_BO_BT_A_T2 with freshABB_pw2_A2 for 5s
heat pw2_BO_BT_A_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw2_A_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_T3 for 720m
pw2_A_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_T3 for 720m

heat pw2_BO_BT_A_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw2_A_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_T3 for 30s
pw2_A_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_T3 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PW2 PAIR: BO + BT, Condition B (BT major, 95%; BO minor, 5%)
// Reciprocal condition. Comparison of A vs B outcomes at 72 h
// determines whether the pair shows history-dependent behaviour.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pw2_BT_major = dispense 19 units of BT_Cells   // 95% component
pw2_BO_minor = dispense 1 units of BO_Cells    // 5% component
abbPW2_B     = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media

pw2_BO_BT_B   = mix pw2_BT_major with pw2_BO_minor for 5s
pw2_BO_BT_B_m = mix pw2_BO_BT_B with abbPW2_B for 5s

pw2_B_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw2_BO_BT_B_m for 720m
pw2_B_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_B_m for 720m

freshABB_pw2_B1 = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw2_BO_BT_B_T2  = mix pw2_BO_BT_B_m with freshABB_pw2_B1 for 5s
heat pw2_BO_BT_B_T2 at 37c for 720m

pw2_B_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw2_BO_BT_B_T2 for 720m
pw2_B_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_B_T2 for 720m

freshABB_pw2_B2 = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
pw2_BO_BT_B_T3  = mix pw2_BO_BT_B_T2 with freshABB_pw2_B2 for 5s
heat pw2_BO_BT_B_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw2_B_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw2_BO_BT_B_T3 for 720m
pw2_B_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_B_T3 for 720m

heat pw2_BO_BT_B_T3 at 37c for 720m

pw2_B_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on pw2_BO_BT_B_T3 for 30s
pw2_B_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_B_T3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB13: pw2QC
// QC gate on PW2 dataset: check that history-dependent
// phenotypes are resolved (difference in species concentrations
// at 72 h between condition A and condition B).
// ============================================================

pw2QCSignal = detect communityCompositionDetection on pw2_BO_BT_A_T3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB14 / BB15: PW2 QC gate
// Pass (BB14): pw2QCSignal > 0 -> PW2 dataset accepted; proceed.
// Fail (BB15): pw2QCSignal <= 0 -> insufficient; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB16 (pw2Join).
// ============================================================

if (pw2QCSignal > 0) {
    dispose pw2_BO_BT_A_T3
    dispose pw2_BO_BT_B_T3
} else {
    drain pw2_BO_BT_A_T3
    drain pw2_BO_BT_B_T3
}

// ============================================================
// BB16: pw2Join
// Dispose PW2 QC signal; proceed to validation branch.
// ============================================================

dispose pw2QCSignal

// ============================================================
// BB17: fullCommunity
// PHASE 4a: Full 12-member community validation.
// All 12 species inoculated at 0.01 OD600 each.
// Total OD600 = 0.12 at t=0. Same serial-transfer protocol.
// Community composition at 72 h compared to gLV model prediction
// trained on T3 (M + PW1 + PW2). Model Pearson r = 0.85 (T3).
// BH, DP encoded via starter cultures prepared in BB1.
//
// NOTE: BU contamination detected at 47.5 h in BU- dropout
// community (0.4% of community, persisting to 2% at 72 h).
// The full community is unaffected; BU- data interpreted with
// this caveat in mind (paper, p. 6).
// ============================================================

// Inoculate all 12 species at 0.01 OD600 from starter cultures.
// Fast-growth: BT, BO, BU, BV, CH, EL (from 16 h starters).
// Slow-growth: BH, FP, CA, PC, ER, DP (from 41 h starters).
abbFull = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media

// Sequential merge: build full community from individual species.
// BioScript does not support n-ary merge; chain binary mixes.
bt_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of BT_Cells
bo_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of BO_Cells
bu_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of BU_Cells
bv_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of BV_Cells
bh_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of BH_Cells
ca_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of CA_Cells
ch_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of CH_Cells
dp_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of DP_Cells
el_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of EL_Cells
er_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of ER_Cells
fp_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of FP_Cells
pc_cells_full  = dispense 1 units of PC_Cells

// Chain merge into full 12-member community droplet.
full_m01 = mix bt_cells_full with bo_cells_full for 5s
full_m02 = mix full_m01 with bu_cells_full for 5s
full_m03 = mix full_m02 with bv_cells_full for 5s
full_m04 = mix full_m03 with bh_cells_full for 5s
full_m05 = mix full_m04 with ca_cells_full for 5s
full_m06 = mix full_m05 with ch_cells_full for 5s
full_m07 = mix full_m06 with dp_cells_full for 5s
full_m08 = mix full_m07 with el_cells_full for 5s
full_m09 = mix full_m08 with er_cells_full for 5s
full_m10 = mix full_m09 with fp_cells_full for 5s
fullCommunity_t0 = mix full_m10 with pc_cells_full for 5s

// Normalise with fresh ABB to consistent total OD600.
fullComm_init = mix fullCommunity_t0 with abbFull for 5s

// Serial transfer 1
full_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on fullComm_init for 720m
full_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on fullComm_init for 720m

freshABB_full1  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
fullComm_T2     = mix fullComm_init with freshABB_full1 for 5s
heat fullComm_T2 at 37c for 720m

// Serial transfer 2
full_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on fullComm_T2 for 720m
full_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on fullComm_T2 for 720m

freshABB_full2  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
fullComm_T3     = mix fullComm_T2 with freshABB_full2 for 5s
heat fullComm_T3 at 37c for 720m

// Serial transfer 3 + final reads
full_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on fullComm_T3 for 720m
full_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on fullComm_T3 for 720m

heat fullComm_T3 at 37c for 720m

full_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on fullComm_T3 for 30s
full_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on fullComm_T3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB18: dropoutCommunity
// PHASE 4b: Single-species dropout community (EL- shown).
// EL- is the most influential dropout: alters community assembly
// more than any other single-species removal (Fig 3B); reduces
// Shannon equitability; reduces community productivity by
// 28-46% across growth stages; reduces growth rate by 19-33%.
// 12 dropout communities total (one per species); EL- encoded
// as representative.
//
// NOTE: The 11-member community is built by omitting EL_Cells
// from the chain merge. All other species at 0.01 OD600.
// ============================================================

abbDropout = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media

bt_drop  = dispense 1 units of BT_Cells
bo_drop  = dispense 1 units of BO_Cells
bu_drop  = dispense 1 units of BU_Cells
bv_drop  = dispense 1 units of BV_Cells
bh_drop  = dispense 1 units of BH_Cells
ca_drop  = dispense 1 units of CA_Cells
ch_drop  = dispense 1 units of CH_Cells
dp_drop  = dispense 1 units of DP_Cells
er_drop  = dispense 1 units of ER_Cells
fp_drop  = dispense 1 units of FP_Cells
pc_drop  = dispense 1 units of PC_Cells

// EL omitted: 11-member community (EL- dropout).
drop_m01 = mix bt_drop with bo_drop for 5s
drop_m02 = mix drop_m01 with bu_drop for 5s
drop_m03 = mix drop_m02 with bv_drop for 5s
drop_m04 = mix drop_m03 with bh_drop for 5s
drop_m05 = mix drop_m04 with ca_drop for 5s
drop_m06 = mix drop_m05 with ch_drop for 5s
drop_m07 = mix drop_m06 with dp_drop for 5s
drop_m08 = mix drop_m07 with er_drop for 5s
drop_m09 = mix drop_m08 with fp_drop for 5s
dropoutEL_t0 = mix drop_m09 with pc_drop for 5s

dropoutEL_init = mix dropoutEL_t0 with abbDropout for 5s

// Serial transfer 1
drop_OD_T1  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on dropoutEL_init for 720m
drop_16S_T1 = detect communityCompositionDetection on dropoutEL_init for 720m

freshABB_drop1  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
dropoutEL_T2    = mix dropoutEL_init with freshABB_drop1 for 5s
heat dropoutEL_T2 at 37c for 720m

// Serial transfer 2
drop_OD_T2  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on dropoutEL_T2 for 720m
drop_16S_T2 = detect communityCompositionDetection on dropoutEL_T2 for 720m

freshABB_drop2  = dispense 19 units of ABB_Media
dropoutEL_T3    = mix dropoutEL_T2 with freshABB_drop2 for 5s
heat dropoutEL_T3 at 37c for 720m

// Serial transfer 3 + final reads
drop_OD_T3  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on dropoutEL_T3 for 720m
drop_16S_T3 = detect communityCompositionDetection on dropoutEL_T3 for 720m

heat dropoutEL_T3 at 37c for 720m

drop_OD_final  = detect monospeciesGrowthDetection on dropoutEL_T3 for 30s
drop_16S_final = detect communityCompositionDetection on dropoutEL_T3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB19: validationQC
// QC gate on Phase 4 communities: Pearson correlation between
// model prediction and experimental data for each species and
// time point must exceed threshold (paper reports median r=0.85
// for T3, with model explaining 81% variance on T4).
// ============================================================

valQCSignal = detect communityCompositionDetection on fullComm_T3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB20 / BB21: Validation QC gate
// Pass (BB20): valQCSignal > 0 -> model validated; proceed.
// Fail (BB21): valQCSignal <= 0 -> validation failed; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB22 (validationJoin).
// ============================================================

if (valQCSignal > 0) {
    dispose fullComm_T3
    dispose dropoutEL_T3
} else {
    drain fullComm_T3
    drain dropoutEL_T3
}

// ============================================================
// BB22: validationJoin
// Dispose validation QC signal; proceed to metabolomics branch.
// ============================================================

dispose valQCSignal

// ============================================================
// BB23: metabolomics
// PHASE 5: Exo-metabolomics profiling (Dataset EV4).
// All 12 monospecies cultured in ABB (ER and FP supplemented
// with 33 mM acetate). Each grown to saturation (72 h, 37 C).
// Diluted to 0.01 OD600; 30 mL replicates (n=3) in 4-well plates.
// Supernatant sampled pre-24 h for each species except DP
// (insufficient biomass within 24 h window).
// Lyophilised, resuspended in MeOH + internal standards.
// LC-MS/MS on Agilent 6550 Q-TOF (HILIC ZIC-pHILIC column).
// 97 metabolites profiled; twofold threshold for significance.
//
// KEY FINDINGS:
//   CH: largest metabolite consumer (hub); not proportional
//       to biomass -> energy diverted to non-growth processes.
//   BU: major metabolite secretor; consistent with large
//       influence on community assembly (Fig 3B).
//   FP: predicted to utilise metabolites from BU, BO, PC, BT,
//       CH -> molecular basis of positive inter-species
//       interactions promoting FP in full community (Fig 5E).
//   EL: metabolite profiles fail to predict EL's influential
//       role -> interactions likely beyond resource competition
//       (biomolecular warfare or toxic metabolite secretion).
//   Resource competition for methyl-5'-thioadenosine (55 pairs),
//   N-methylanthranilic acid (6 pairs), dihexose (3 pairs).
//
// BIOSCRIPT ENCODING:
//   Each monospecies produces a conditioned media droplet (CM).
//   exoMetabolomicsDetection module abstracts LC-MS/MS readout.
//   DP is excluded (paper: insufficient biomass within 24 h).
// ============================================================

// Prepare monospecies for metabolomics: saturation culture + dilution.
// Each species grown 72 h to saturation then diluted to 0.01 OD600.

meta_BT_sat  = dispense 1 units of BT_Cells
abbMeta_BT   = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
metaBT       = mix meta_BT_sat with abbMeta_BT for 5s
heat metaBT at 37c for 4320m  // 72 h saturation = 4320 m

meta_FP_sat  = dispense 1 units of FP_Cells
abbMeta_FP   = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
metaFP       = mix meta_FP_sat with abbMeta_FP for 5s
heat metaFP at 37c for 4320m

meta_EL_sat  = dispense 1 units of EL_Cells
abbMeta_EL   = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
metaEL       = mix meta_EL_sat with abbMeta_EL for 5s
heat metaEL at 37c for 4320m

meta_BU_sat  = dispense 1 units of BU_Cells
abbMeta_BU   = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
metaBU       = mix meta_BU_sat with abbMeta_BU for 5s
heat metaBU at 37c for 4320m

meta_CH_sat  = dispense 1 units of CH_Cells
abbMeta_CH   = dispense 1 units of ABB_Media
metaCH       = mix meta_CH_sat with abbMeta_CH for 5s
heat metaCH at 37c for 4320m

// Collect supernatants (t=0 and pre-24 h time point).
// exoMetabolomicsDetection abstracts: centrifuge (6000g, 5 min),
// 0.22 um filtration, lyophilisation, MeOH resuspension,
// LC-MS/MS run, metabolite atlas peak annotation.

metaBT_signal  = detect exoMetabolomicsDetection on metaBT for 30s
metaFP_signal  = detect exoMetabolomicsDetection on metaFP for 30s
metaEL_signal  = detect exoMetabolomicsDetection on metaEL for 30s
metaBU_signal  = detect exoMetabolomicsDetection on metaBU for 30s
metaCH_signal  = detect exoMetabolomicsDetection on metaCH for 30s

// NOTE: BO, BV, BH, CA, ER, PC monospecies metabolomics follow
// the identical dispense -> heat 4320m -> detect pattern.
// Omitted for brevity but required for full Dataset EV4.
// DP is omitted entirely (paper M&M: insufficient biomass).

// ============================================================
// BB24: metaQC
// QC gate on metabolomics dataset: check that at least twofold
// changes in metabolite abundances are resolved for the majority
// of the 97 targeted metabolites across at least 3 replicates.
// ============================================================

metaQCSignal = detect exoMetabolomicsDetection on metaCH for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB25 / BB26: Metabolomics QC gate
// Pass (BB25): metaQCSignal > 0 -> metabolomics data accepted.
// Fail (BB26): metaQCSignal <= 0 -> LC-MS/MS failure; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB27 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (metaQCSignal > 0) {
    dispose metaBT
    dispose metaFP
    dispose metaEL
    dispose metaBU
    dispose metaCH
} else {
    drain metaBT
    drain metaFP
    drain metaEL
    drain metaBU
    drain metaCH
}

// ============================================================
// BB27: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// All five experimental phases (M, PW1, PW2, validation,
// metabolomics) complete. gLV model training datasets (T1-T3)
// and validation datasets are ready for parameter estimation
// and MCMC uncertainty analysis (paper Section 2.3/2.4).
// ============================================================

dispose metaBT_signal
dispose metaFP_signal
dispose metaEL_signal
dispose metaBU_signal
dispose metaCH_signal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
